    "turn_text": "You can put things into three buckets. Bucket one is interfering with the actual vote tally. that Joe Jones votes for Senator Smith, and instead the vote gets registered as for Senator Johnson. So you're like hacking the voting, you're hacking the voting machines, you're interfering with the integrity of the transmission of the vote. That I think we seem to be fairly well on top of, and we get good reports about being on top of that from the intelligence community, and there's no known instance of that happening. So it's something to watch, but I think we're in reasonably good shape. The second is political money flowing into us. And unfortunately, we are very vulnerable still in that area. We maintain a whole variety of mechanisms for dark money to flow into American elections. donor advised trusts 501c4 shell corporations all of that sadly there is a domestic constituency for that of big special interests who want to hide their own hands while they play in our politics, but the problem is that once you have a channel that is, that provides anonymity, you can't distinguish between who is an anonymous domestic influencer,",
