  {
    "episode_id": 82290,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/2/82290.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 77,
    "turn_text": "It's really rewarding. Frustrating as hell. sometimes, but rewarding. Plus, this is the United States of America. We are different, exceptional, and special in my view. And to be a part of that is to dedicate yourself to a cause that matters. So, doubly do it. Read, read, read. I think is really good advice and listen, listen, listen, and don't think that some task or some role is not grand enough for you. Start at the City Council. Start working for a state representative. Start wherever. And then when you're doing what you're doing, distinguish yourself by working hard, being honorable, and showing up on time. And if you can do simple tasks like that and persist at it, people notice, and next thing you know you're asked to do something more important. And then you do that again, and next thing you know you're asked to do something more important. It gets very rewarding very quickly.",
